   "he": "וּמִלְּעָרֵב. אָמְרִי דְּבֵי רַבִּי יַנַּאי: לֹא שָׁנוּ אֶלָּא עֵירוּבֵי חֲצֵירוֹת, אֲבָל עֵירוּבֵי תְּחוּמִין חַיָּיבִין.",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: «And» in a military camp, one is exempt «from establishing an eiruv.» The Sages of «the school of Rabbi Yannai said: They taught» that this exemption applies «only» with regard to «the joining of» houses in «courtyards. However,» even those in a military encampment «are obligated» to establish an eiruv if they desire to effect «a joining of Shabbat boundaries,» whereby one extends the Shabbat limits beyond which one may not walk on Shabbat."
  }
